-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:710de5f0be72f6ef5d891a806f2f59376362c605d7cef49b3ad03b4c3238014e","file":"preprints/A-high-arity-counterexample-to-Pixton-completeness-in-Chow-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":76,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"b3e54d8d33a98c0a39512cc3dbe18216f9f7426bd20d415d4c4e80d777a361fc","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-high-arity-counterexample-to-Pixton-completeness-in-Chow-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:710de5f0be72f6ef5d891a806f2f59376362c605d7cef49b3ad03b4c3238014e","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-high-arity-counterexample-to-Pixton-completeness-in-Chow-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L76"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nSet\n\\[\ng=10^{60},\\qquad D_*=\\binom g3,\\qquad n=3D_*.\n\\]\nThe explicitly defined class \\(Y\\in \\Salg_{g,n}^{2D_*}\\) of\nDefinition~\\ref{def:candidate} satisfies\n\\[\nq_{g,n}(Y)=0,\\qquad Y\\notin\\Pspan_{g,n}.\n\\]\nConsequently Pixton's original relation span does not exhaust the\ntautological Chow relations: the equality\n\\(\\ker q_{g,n}=\\Pspan_{g,n}\\) fails for this stable pair."}
